# Next.js 16

This project uses **Next.js 16** with App Router. Read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before writing route code — APIs may differ from training data.

## Params are Promises

```typescript
// ✅ Next.js 16 — params is a Promise
const { id } = await params;

// ❌ Old pattern — will break
const { id } = params;
```

## Page structure

```typescript
export const revalidate = 60; // ISR — use static by default, dynamic only when needed

export async function generateMetadata({ params }: Props): Promise<Metadata> {
  // Always include: title, description, canonical, OG, twitter, JSON-LD
}

export default async function Page({ params }: Props) {
  // Server Component — fetch via services, pass props to *Client.tsx
}
```

## Rendering strategy

1. **Static** (default) — prefer ISR with `revalidate`
2. **Dynamic** — only when user-specific data can't be split to client
3. **Streaming** — provide `loading.tsx` for every route group

## Route protection

- `src/proxy.ts` (Next.js 16 proxy) — not legacy `middleware.ts`
- Dashboard: `auth()` + `redirect("/login")` in layout
- Admin: `notFound()` for non-admin users
- Private pages: `robots: { index: false }`

## Use when appropriate

- Route Groups for shared layouts
- Parallel Routes for dashboard panels
- Intercepting Routes for modals
- Server Actions for mutations
- Metadata API for SEO (never manual `<meta>` tags)
